Overview
In this challenge lab, you are tasked with evaluating and hill climbing a Generative AI agent using autoraters. Building real-world AI agents requires rigorous, scalable evaluation to ensure consistent and reliable outputs. You run evaluation pipelines using the Gen AI evaluation service on Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform, analyze autorater self-consistency, and iteratively hill climb the agent's output quality until it passes the autoraters.

Objectives
In this challenge lab, you demonstrate your ability to do the following:

Interpret and apply inter-/intra-rater reliability metrics.
Distinguish between useful metrics and distractors for assessing autorater self-consistency.
Utilize the outputs of autoraters to assess agent performance.
Navigate ADK's built-in tools to diagnose agent malfunctions.
Improve agent skills based on evaluation feedback.
